#. type: Title ===
#: pages/fca.adoc:148
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why so many titles?"
msgstr "Varför så många titlar?"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/fca.adoc:157
msgid ""
"The title of this role evolved and changed over the years since its "
"inception in February 2015.  The creation of the role was largely envisioned"
" and advocated for by xref:fpl.adoc#previous[Robyn Bergeron], then the "
"Fedora Project Leader.  When the role was first created, the role title was "
"https://fedoramagazine.org/fedora-community-action-and-impact-job-opening-"
"red-hat-osas/[*Fedora Community Outreach and Impact Lead*], which was often "
"shortened to Fedora Community Lead (FCL).  At the time, the FCL role "
"provided needed separation of responsibilities with the xref:fpl.adoc[Fedora"
" Project Leader], including the role of organizing the annual Fedora "
"contributor conference, Flock.  However, the FCL title did not feel totally "
"right either.  Anyone can be a leader in the Fedora community, whether they "
"are employed by Red Hat or not! We did not want to imply otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Titeln för denna roll har utvecklats och ändrats under åren sedan den "
"skapades i februari 2015.  Rollen utformades och drevs i hög grad av "
"xref:fpl.adoc#previous[Robyn Bergeron], dåvarande Fedora Project Leader.  "
"När rollen först skapades hette den https://fedoramagazine.org/fedora-"
"community-action-and-impact-job-opening-red-hat-osas/[*Fedora Community "
"Outreach and Impact Lead*], ofta förkortat Fedora Community Lead (FCL).  Vid"
" den tiden innebar FCL-rollen en nödvändig uppdelning av ansvaret jämfört "
"med xref:fpl.adoc[Fedora Project Leader], bland annat ansvaret för att "
"arrangera den årliga Fedora-konferensen Flock.  Men FCL-titeln kändes inte "
"heller helt rätt.  Vem som helst kan vara ledare i Fedora-gemenskapen, "
"oavsett om personen är anställd av Red Hat eller inte! Vi ville inte antyda "
"något annat."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/fca.adoc:163
msgid ""
"Later, in October 2016, the role title was changed to *Fedora Community "
"Action & Impact Coordinator* (FCAIC).  This title was lengthier but better "
"captured what community engagement means in a large, globally-distributed "
"community like Fedora.  Over time, more projects, organizations, and "
"companies working on Free & Open Source Software (FOSS) introduced new roles"
" in community management and leadership.  However, community work does not "
"have an industry-accepted job ladder, as is more common with software "
"engineering.  Red Hat eventually settled on the title of _community "
"architect_ for a career path in community management in its pioneering Open "
"Source communities."
msgstr ""
"Senare, i oktober 2016, ändrades rolltiteln till *Fedora Community Action & "
"Impact Coordinator* (FCAIC).  Titeln var längre men beskrev bättre vad "
"engagemang i gemenskapen innebär i en stor, globalt spridd gemenskap som "
"Fedora.  Med tiden infördes nya roller inom community management och "
"ledarskap av fler projekt, organisationer och företag som arbetar med fri "
"programvara med öppen källkod (FOSS).  Gemenskapsarbete har dock ingen "
"allmänt erkänd yrkesstege, vilket är vanligare inom programvaruutveckling.  "
"Red Hat valde till slut titeln _community architect_ för en karriärväg inom "
"community management i sina banbrytande öppen källkod-gemenskaper."

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/fca.adoc:168
msgid ""
"The title was changed in January 2023 to *Fedora Community Architect* (FCA) "
"to reflect the changing landscape.  Ultimately, the goal of changing the "
"name then was to better describe the role and what the FCA did in Fedora.  "
"The lengthy \"FCAIC\" title often came with an explanation to others "
"unfamiliar with Fedora and our unique community culture.  FCA was also a "
"handy shortening of the longer FCAIC acronym too!"
msgstr ""
"Titeln ändrades i januari 2023 till *Fedora Community Architect* (FCA) för "
"att spegla det förändrade landskapet.  Syftet var att bättre beskriva rollen"
" och vad FCA gör i Fedora.  Den långa titeln ”FCAIC” krävde ofta en "
"förklaring för personer som inte kände till Fedora och vår särskilda "
"gemenskapskultur.  FCA blev också en praktisk förkortning av den längre "
"akronymen FCAIC."

#. type: Title ===
#: pages/fca.adoc:170
#, no-wrap
msgid "2026 role changes"
msgstr "Rolländringar 2026"

#. type: Plain text
#: pages/fca.adoc:176
msgid ""
"In 2026, this charter was substantially rewritten to describe the FCA's "
"actual scope of work, rather than the broader \"community manager\" framing "
"it had carried since the role's earliest days.  <<roles,_Roles and "
"Responsibilities_>> was reorganized around four concrete areas — <<roles-"
"governance,_Council governance_>>, <<roles-budget,_budget and fiduciary "
"stewardship_>>, the <<roles-flock,_Flock conference_>>, and <<roles-"
"centos,_CentOS ecosystem_>> — with CentOS added as a newly explicit "
"responsibility, reflecting the deepening relationship between Fedora and its"
" sibling project.  The _Community Initiative Support_ and _Collaboration "
"with Community Ops_ sections were removed — the former because the Fedora "
"Council paused the Community Initiatives program, and the latter because "
"supporting Community Ops was never a distinct, formal responsibility of the "
"role.  <<decision-making,_Decision-Making_>> was expanded to state plainly "
"that the FCA, while a Red Hat employee, is a fiduciary for the Fedora "
"Project: the community budget belongs to Red Hat, but its stewardship serves"
" Fedora.  The FCA's ongoing working relationship with the Fedora Project "
"Leader and Fedora Operations Architect was documented for the first time, "
"and the stakeholder list in <<communication,_Communication_>> was tightened "
"to reflect only the relationships tied to a formal responsibility."
msgstr ""
"År 2026 skrevs denna stadga om i grunden för att beskriva FCA:s faktiska "
"arbetsområde, i stället för den bredare inramning som ”community manager” "
"som den hade haft sedan rollens första dagar.  <<roles,_Roller och ansvar_>>"
" omorganiserades kring fyra konkreta områden – <<roles-governance,_rådets "
"styrning_>>, <<roles-budget,_budget och förvaltaransvar_>>, <<roles-"
"flock,_Flock-konferensen_>> och <<roles-centos,_CentOS-ekosystemet_>> – och "
"CentOS lades till som ett nytt uttryckligt ansvar, vilket återspeglar det "
"fördjupade förhållandet mellan Fedora och dess systerprojekt.  Avsnitten "
"_Stöd till community initiatives_ och _Samarbete med Community Ops_ togs "
"bort – det första eftersom Fedora Council pausade programmet Community "
"Initiatives och det andra eftersom stöd till Community Ops aldrig var ett "
"separat, formellt ansvar för rollen.  <<decision-making,_Beslutsfattande_>> "
"utökades för att tydligt slå fast att FCA, trots att rollen är anställd av "
"Red Hat, är förvaltare för Fedora-projektet: gemenskapsbudgeten tillhör Red "
"Hat, men dess förvaltning tjänar Fedora.  FCA:s fortlöpande samarbete med "
"Fedora Project Leader och Fedora Operations Architect dokumenterades för "
"första gången, och intressentlistan i <<communication,_Kommunikation_>> "
"begränsades så att den bara omfattar relationer som är knutna till ett "
"formellt ansvar."
